The IsTransient predicate returns true whenever the entity has been recently created
and hasn't been recorded in the permanent storage, so its primary key is still undefined.
In .NET, it is good practice that, whenever you override
the Object.Equal method of a class, you also override its
Object.GetHashCode method so that class instances can be efficiently
stored in data structures such as dictionaries and sets. That's why the
Entity class overrides it.
It is also worth implementing an IEntity<K> interface that defines all the
